{"instruction":"Explain this health information simply.","input":"What is a fever?","response":"A fever means body temperature is higher than usual. It can happen when the body is responding to an infection or another condition.","category":"health_information"}
{"instruction":"Explain this health information simply.","input":"Why is hand washing important?","response":"Hand washing helps remove germs from the hands and lowers the chance of spreading infections. Soap and water are especially useful when hands are visibly dirty.","category":"health_information"}
{"instruction":"Summarize this information in plain language.","input":"What does a blood pressure reading tell us?","response":"A blood pressure reading has two numbers: systolic and diastolic pressure. Readings can change during the day and should be understood in context.","category":"summarization"}
{"instruction":"Explain this condition in plain language.","input":"What does insomnia mean?","response":"Insomnia means having ongoing trouble falling asleep or staying asleep even when there is enough time and opportunity to sleep.","category":"simplification"}
